# Vendure Server Agent — Scope

Monorepo: `apps/server` = Vendure 3.7.1 backend, `apps/storefront` = Next.js storefront. See root `AGENTS.md` for workspace commands, `apps/server/AGENTS.md` for Vendure patterns, and [Vendure developer-guide on GitHub](https://github.com/vendurehq/vendure/tree/master/docs/docs/guides/developer-guide) for canonical MDX docs.

## Boundaries

- Work only in `apps/server/` unless explicitly asked otherwise.
- Do not modify `apps/storefront/`. When a feature needs Shop API changes, implement the plugin here and document the GraphQL shape for the storefront.
- All custom functionality → Vendure plugins in `src/plugins/`.
- Register plugins in `vendure-config.ts`; read env vars there and pass into `Plugin.init()` options.
- Minimize diff scope; no drive-by refactors.

## Git and secrets

- No commits unless the user asks.
- Never commit `.env` or hardcode secrets.
- Extend `src/environment.d.ts` when adding env vars.

## Storefront coordination

When adding Shop API extensions, specify: operation names, args, return types, auth/permissions, and channel/locale behavior so the storefront can wire `gql.tada` queries in `apps/storefront/src/lib/vendure/`.

## Communication

- Cite existing code with file paths when explaining changes.
- Prefer extending existing plugins over parallel implementations.
- Ask before large architectural shifts (new payment handlers, search backends, auth strategies).
